body:
I use these dust bags with my HEPA filter-equipped Miele Titan Classic canister vac (

New Miele Classic C1 Titan Canister Vacuum, Mango Red

), which I really love. Any vacuum's performance is limited by the quality of the dust bags used, and I'm willing to pay more for better performance. These genuine Miele bags permit objectively better cleaning than the off-label aftermarket bags I once tried in an effort to economize. Those bags might have been almost half the price, but they lasted only a fraction as long as the AirClean 3D bags do and didn't perform well for long. In fact, I have been absolutely gobsmacked by the amount of dirt and debris the AirClean 3D bags pack in before the vacuum's suction wanes noticeably when a new bag is needed. The build quality of these dust bags is exceptional- I can't imagine having one rip or rupture during removal (even when jam-packed with crud)- and bag replacement is a snap, as long as the bag isn't overly full. All that said, I have two minor gripes, which explain the 4-star rating: 1) when the bag gets really full, it can be like a very dense foam pillow, which makes it tough to get out of the vacuum and invariably allows some of the filthy contents escape (this is partly an operator problem- I should change the bag earlier); and 2) these ARE kind of expensive for vacuum bags. On the other hand, why compromise the performance of a $500 vacuum cleaner with a cheap, ineffective bag?
